00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.380
Now, let's start the video....

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.700
The very first question; What is NCB?

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.375
The NCB is called NO Claim Bonus.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.385
Which is an award or discount provided to the Insured person

00:01:06.385 --> 00:01:09.255
by the company.

00:01:09.255 --> 00:01:12.135
If the owner of the vehicle has not made any claim,

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.200
during the policy period or Twelve months.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.400
A discount is offered at the time of renewal of the policy.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.155
Because you have not made any claim...

00:01:21.155 --> 00:01:24.055
and You have benefited the company. So, the company offers a discount.

00:01:24.055 --> 00:01:26.695
When and how much NCB discount is offered?

00:01:26.695 --> 00:01:29.545
NCB is a discount is provided as per this table.

00:01:29.545 --> 00:01:32.035
If you have not made any claim during the preceding ...full year of insurance.

00:01:32.035 --> 00:01:35.105
So at the time of policy renewal for the next year, you will get 20% NCB Discount.

00:01:35.105 --> 00:01:37.885
If you don't claim in the one more next year,

00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:40.985
then at the time of second-time policy renewal

00:01:40.985 --> 00:01:42.420
you will get a 25% NCB Discount.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.560
Likewise, if you don't claim for the preceding five years

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.775
at the time of policy renewal for the sixth year,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.905
you will get a 50% NCB discount.

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:55.920
The NCB discount can be a maximum of 50%

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.535
it will not go more than 50%, but...

00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:01.595
meanwhile, if you made any claim.

00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:04.745
Suppose, in the sixth year, you made with an accident and you claim.

00:02:04.745 --> 00:02:07.755
Then you NCB will be cancelled or become zero.

00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:10.915
Now, you have to earn it again by making no claim.

00:02:10.915 --> 00:02:13.915
If you don't claim in the seventh year, you will earn 20% NCB.

00:02:13.915 --> 00:02:17.005
Now, is this NCB discount is applicable on the total premium?

00:02:17.005 --> 00:02:19.855
The 20%,  35% or 50% NCB,

00:02:19.855 --> 00:02:22.865
Does it mean you will have to pay only

00:02:22.865 --> 00:02:25.885
50% of the net premium of the policy?

00:02:25.885 --> 00:02:28.805
the answer is, NO. as the NCB is computed only on OD premium.

00:02:28.805 --> 00:02:31.825
or the Own Damage premium component.

00:02:31.825 --> 00:02:34.855
We can understand it like;

00:02:34.855 --> 00:02:38.285
there are a lot of coverages in our policy

00:02:38.285 --> 00:02:41.595
the net premium is calculated by adding all components of the premium of different covers.

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:44.675
So the premium component which

00:02:44.675 --> 00:02:47.445
covers only your vehicle,

00:02:47.445 --> 00:02:50.465
or it is called Basic OD [Own Damage] Premium

00:02:50.465 --> 00:02:53.315
The NCB Discount percentage,

00:02:53.315 --> 00:02:56.355
is to be computed on this Basic OD Premium factor.

00:02:56.355 --> 00:02:59.045
For better understanding let's take an example of a policy.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:02.440
This is an ICIC Lombard Zero Dep. car policy.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:06.840
As you can see the total premium is INR Rs. 31,910/

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.275
But the policy has two sections.

00:03:08.275 --> 00:03:10.885
The one is A section or the Own Damage section

00:03:10.885 --> 00:03:13.615
Which is related to your own vehicle covers

00:03:13.615 --> 00:03:15.955
Our vehicle, or any other our mishaps.

00:03:15.955 --> 00:03:19.045
The second section is the B section or third party section

00:03:19.045 --> 00:03:20.560
or the Liability section.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:25.080
So, in the OD section, there is Zero Dep. cover

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.320
and 5670 Rs. for Zero dep. cover

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.780
1638 Rs. is for the cover for consumables

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.680
and Rs. 14743 is for the Basic OD premium.

00:03:34.075 --> 00:03:37.015
So the 20% NCB in the policy,

00:03:37.015 --> 00:03:39.575
will be calculated on Basic OD premium

00:03:39.575 --> 00:03:42.865
and that is Rs. 14743.

00:03:42.865 --> 00:03:45.765
So, 20% of Rs. 14743 is Rs. 2948.6

00:03:45.765 --> 00:03:48.495
So the discount here is Rs. 2949

00:03:48.495 --> 00:03:50.605
is provided as the no claim bonus.

00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:53.425
and not getting 20% of the total premium.

00:03:53.795 --> 00:03:56.775
likewise, if NCB would be 50% then we would be getting is 50% of the Basic OD premium not of the total.

00:03:56.775 --> 00:03:59.605
Here OD Premium is Rs. 14743 so,

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:03.660
we would be getting around Rs. 7371.5

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.080
When can we get the benefit of NCB?

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.540
The benefit of NCB is availed at the time of the renewal of the policy.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:11.480
after twelve months of the policy without making any claim.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.380
But if...

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.820
You forgot to take the benefit at the time of renewal of the policy,

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.360
You can take at later on as well.

00:04:20.365 --> 00:04:23.115
Company will return you the access amount paid by you,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.140
or the NCB discount amount.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.620
Now, if the policy is expired.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.900
will you get NCB discount or not?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.440
So, if your policy is expired in the last 45 days.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.340
and you are renewing the policy within 45 days.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.020
then you will get the NCB Benefit.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:44.740
But...

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.060
If your policy is expired more than 45 days ago.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.785
No claim bonus will be cancelled and you can not get it.

00:04:51.785 --> 00:04:55.560
Q. If you have sold out your vehicle, how the NCB is transferred?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.340
Will the NCB transferred to you or the buyer?

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.145
we can understand it simply by the fact that.

00:05:01.145 --> 00:05:05.240
the NCB is entitled to the Insured person,

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.360
Not the vehicle or the policy.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.580
So, when you sell your vehicle, the NCB will be with you.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.820
Whenever you buy a new vehicle.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.880
You can get the benefit of the NCB in the policy of that new vehicle.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.920
It should be availed withing THREE Years.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.480
You can buy a new vehicle within the next THREE years

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.700
 

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.925
and get your NCB benefit transferred to that policy

00:05:28.925 --> 00:05:31.935
Q. If we select more NCB at the time of renewal of the policy?

00:05:31.935 --> 00:05:34.995
Suppose you are eligible to get 35% NCB discount,

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:41.340
and you select it 45% or 50%

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:45.760
Then the company will issue an NCB Recovery letter and send it to you.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.240
and whatever the more NCB benefit you have availed,

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.160
You will have to pay it to the company.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.700
Otherwise, your policy may be canceled.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.100
Before this notice, you make any claim

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.080
or you made with any accident then,

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.860
Then you claim will not be processed until

00:06:03.865 --> 00:06:07.140
You pay that amount.

